  "_comment_pages": "Page sizes are PER PAGE, not global: pages 1-4 are portrait 816x1056 and page 5 — the financing annex — is landscape 1056x816. `layout.placeText` flips the baseline against the page it draws on, so a single global height would scatter every field on page 5 off the sheet with no error raised.",
  "_comment_row": "`row` groups fields that must share one type size. Only the five instalment columns use it: they are 176 wide, and from the 12-panel tier up the 12-month payment crosses into five digits and measures 183 at 36pt while its four neighbours measure ~162. Fitting each on its own would print one column at 34.5pt beside four at 36pt. See layout.fitRowSize.",
